{
  "dom_id": "step-q182025",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A=\\{4,\\,1,\\,-2,\\,-5,\\,…\\}?$\n\nThe set has no {{field-1}}, while the {{field-2}} is {{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nNotice that elements of $A$ form an infinite, decreasing arithmetic sequence. \n\nTherefore, this set has $\\text{no minimum},$ while \n\n$$\nmax(A)=max\\{4,\\,1,\\,-2,\\,-5,\\,…\\}=4.\n$$",
